<p>I don't really have much to add here that isn't very similar to what the other people here are saying.</p>
<p>Your idea isn't exactly an original one on the Site, as Grigori Karpin pointed out, and to back up their point, allow me to point you to <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4039">this article</a>: the Second Second Law of Thermodynamics. Other than the primary anomaly (and some differences in story), your idea is almost exactly the same as that one.</p>
<p>I'd suggest finding something to differentiate your idea from SCP-4039. If you can't or won't, I'd personally recommend scrapping this idea due to how difficult it would be to execute it successfully without looking like a clone of the aforementioned SCP.</p>
<p>I'd also suggest checking out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for some great essays on ideation, narrative writing/structure, and much more!</p>
<p>Anyway, that's it for my crit. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps.</p>

