					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/teproxy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3047591); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3047591&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606376505" alt="teproxy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3047591)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/teproxy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3047591); return false;" >teproxy</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606376093 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Nov 2020 07:34</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-5494/comments/show">SCP-5494</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828359">
									

<p>i'm conflicted about this. prose is good, concept is good, formatting is good. but this work is *political* and that means i can analyse the *politics*.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;so&nbsp;here's&nbsp;the&nbsp;thing</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;if&nbsp;you&nbsp;care&nbsp;to&nbsp;read</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>you nailed the tone, and how a work like this really ought to go&#8230; in addendum 2. the rest felt kind of off.</p>
<p>basically this handled the message of &quot;racism against first nations is bad&quot; way better than the complicated matter of genuine colonialism.</p>
<p>the former was crystal clear. incompetent and racist government, huge anti-indigenous sentiment, the foundation being ignorant but otherwise impartial. i'm also going to go against the grain and say that scout's final message was actually good, and worked in-universe.</p>
<p>the latter&#8230; was messy. i got it, but it was messy. the expropriation of land (which happened, but they made up for it by helping those who were persecuted), listening to indigenous voices (which you are not, i am not, and of which there were none in the work), cultural appropriation (i don't think this work is that, but you and i both know it's mighty fucking close).</p>
<p>it's hard to mix that tight-rope with a feel-good story about overcoming ignorance, helping first nations people, respecting culture, etc.</p>
<p>i frankly don't think you pulled that aspect off. not bad, but only good. it's fundamentally a story about two important named scientists with lives and histories, and The Natives Of The Region. that's fair. you are only really able to tell the parts of the story here that are yours to tell. that makes it weak, but it's not strictly your fault. you're self-aware based on your other comments, too, which is good.</p>
<p>i am curious to see what you do next, and how your social commentary matures, especially if you venture into matters which you are more <em>personally</em> familiar with.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>overall though, this was above average in all other regards. +1</p>

							</div>

								
					
